  "Question": "A dress originally priced at \\(\\$80\\) was put on sale at \\(25\\%\\) off. If \\(10\\%\\) tax was added to the sale price, then the total selling price of the dress was",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\$45\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\$52\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\$54\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\$66\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\$68\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The tax is based on the sale price, so first find the price after the discount. The \\(25\\%\\) discount is\n\\[\n0.25\\cdot80=20\n\\]\ndollars, leaving a sale price of \\(80-20=60\\) dollars. The tax is then \\(10\\%\\) of \\(60\\), which is \\(0.10\\cdot60=6\\) dollars. Thus the total selling price is\n\\[\n60+6=66\n\\]\ndollars, or \\(\\$66\\), choice D.",
